  glossary: {
    /* ---- war machine weapon profiles (from the source PDF) ---- */
    "Leadbelcher Gun": `Leadbelcher guns have the following profile: Range 12/24", Strength 5, Special Rules: Multiple Shots (D6), Rapid Fire, Slow to Fire.`,
    "Scraplauncher Catapult": `A scraplauncher catapult is a stone thrower with the following profile: Range 12-48", Strength 3(3), Special Rules: Cumbersome, Killing Blow.`,
    "Skewerslinger Bolt Thrower": `A skewerslinger is a bolt thrower with the following profile: Range 48", Strength 6, Special Rules: Cumbersome, Multiple Shots (D3), Multiple Wounds (D3), Rapid Fire. The Skewerslinger does not suffer To Hit penalties for moving and shooting.`,
    "Cannon of the Sky-titans": `A cannon of the Sky-titans is a great cannon with the following profile: Range 12-72", Strength 10, Special Rules: Cumbersome, Multiple Wounds (D6). When rolling to determine the bounce distance, roll the artillery dice twice and use the highest roll; grapeshot fired by it is Strength 10.`,
    "Chaintrap": `A chaintrap has the following profile: Range 6/9", Strength 6, Special Rules: Killing Blow, Quick Shot.`,
    "Harpoon Launcher": `A harpoon launcher has the following profile: Range 28/42", Strength 5, Special Rules: Multiple Wounds (D3), Ponderous.`,
    /* auto-mapped from army-book PDF (unit UPGRADE / option rules) */
    "Belligerent Charger": `The Stonehorn may re-roll failed charge distances. However, it is also subject to the Berserk Rage part of Frenzy.`,
    "Fleshgreed": `Whenever the Thundertusk inflicts an unsaved Wound in close combat, roll a D6; on a natural 6, they regain one Wound lost previously during the game. This has no effect on Animated Constructs, Daemons, Forest Spirits or Vampires.`,
    "Rimefrost Hide": `The Thundertusk gains the Natural Armour (6+) special rule.`,
    "Rockmane Elder": `All attacks targeting the Stonehorn suffer -1 To Wound.`,

    /* auto-mapped from army-book PDF (unit-profile special rules) */
    "Avatar of the Fire Mouth": `When Morg suffers an unsaved wound in close combat, enemy models in base contact suffer a Strength 4 Hit with the Flaming Attacks special rule. When Morg is slain, place the small template above him. All models underneath the template suffer a Strength 4 hit with the Flaming Attacks special rule.`,
    "Everyone Has Their Price": `At the start of each enemy turn (before any Stupidity tests are taken) you can nominate D3 enemy units that are within 18" of Greasus to have the Stupidity special rule for the remainder of the turn. This ability has no effect on units that have Immunity (Psychology).`,
    "Fall Over": `A Giant must test to see whether it falls over if any of the following apply: - If it is beaten in close combat. Test once results are established but before taking a Break test. - If it is fleeing at the start of the Movement phase. - When it crosses an obstacle. Test when the obstacle is reached. - If the Giant decides to Jump Up and Down on an enemy. Test immediately beforehand.`,
    "Fire Breath": `A model with this special rule has a Strength 3 Breath Weapon with the Flaming Attacks special rule.`,
    "Giant Special Attacks": `To determine what a Giant does in each Close Combat phase, pick a unit in base contact with the Giant and roll a D6 on one of the following tables. Which table you use depends on the size of the Giant's victim. If no suitable target is in base contact, roll again on the chart until you get another result.`,
    "Hoardmaster": `Unless Greasus is fleeing, all friendly units within 18" of Greasus (including the Overtyrant himself), add +1 to their combat result scores.`,
    "Hunt-father": `Jhared may re-roll To Hit and to Wound rolls of 1 when fighting War Beasts, Monstrous Beasts, Monstrous Cavalry, Monstrous Creatures and Monsters. In addition, he ignores Terror caused by Monstrous Creatures and Monsters.`,
    "Ice Breath": `Rimespeakers have a Strength 3 Breath Weapon with the Ice Attacks and Magical Attacks special rules.`,
    "Iron Rhinox": `The Iron Rhinox has a Strength 2 Breath Weapon with the Armour Piercing (2) special rule.`,
    "Mammoth Attacks": `When the Ice Mammoth attacks, roll on the appropriate following table to determine its action. If no suitable target is in base contact, roll again on the chart until you get another result.`,
    "Slavelord": `Braugh begins the game with 12 slaves, these must form up with Braugh placed in the centre of the unit. Braugh benefits from "Look Out, Sir!" as long as there are at least 5 slaves in the unit. He may not voluntarily leave the unit under any circumstances. In addition, as long as Braugh is alive, all slaves have the Regeneration (5+) and Stubborn special rules.`,
    "The First Butcher": `Once per turn, Groth may re-roll a dice when casting a spell or when trying to dispel an enemy spell.`,
    "The Goldtooth Tribe": `At least one unit of Ironguts must be included in an army led by Greasus.`,
    "The Ironskin Tribe": `If Ghark is the Army General, Leadbelchers count as a Core Units instead of Special Units and Grimhorn Rhinox Riders count as a Special Units instead of Rare Units.`,
    "The Lazarghs": `Choose one unit of Ogre Bulls or Ironguts in an army including Groth. This unit causes Terror instead of Fear.`,

    "Beneath Contempt": `Gnoblars have the Expendable special rule. In addition, even other Gnoblars treat them as being Expendable.`,
    "Bicker": `Roll a D6 at the beginning of each of your turns for each unit with this special rule that is not in combat or fleeing and has a Unit Strength of 5 or more. If a unit rolls a 1 it may not move in the Movement phase or shoot in the Shooting phase this turn.`,
    "Ogre Charge": `Each model on foot with the Ogre Charge special rule that successfully charges an enemy has the Impact Hits (1) special rule. Models with this special rule that are part of a unit with ranks add their current Rank Bonus to the Strength of the Impact Hits they inflict. In addition, they count as having one more rank than their actual number for the purpose of determining Steadfast in any turn that they charge.`,
    "Gutplate": `A model with a gutplate gains a 6+ armour save against attacks to the front.`,
    "Ironfist": `Buckler. If a model with an ironfist rolls a natural 6 when making a Parry save, it automatically inflicts an extra Hit back onto the model or unit that struck the blow. In addition, a model using an ironfist benefits from the Parry special rule even while mounted.`,
    "Blood Vulture": `Treated as a missile weapon. Range 24", Strength 4, Sniper. Rather than rolling to Hit using Ballistic Skill, the target must pass a Weapon Skill test to avoid being Hit.`,
    "Chaintrap": `Range 6/9", Strength 6, Killing Blow, Quick Shot.`,
    "Harpoon Launcher": `Range 28/42", Strength 5, Multiple Wounds (D3), Ponderous.`,
    "Ogre Pistol": `Range 12/24", Strength 5. Brace: Multiple Shots (2), Quick Shot.`,
    "Oriental Longsword": `Combat, As user Strength, Parry (6+), +1 To Wound.`,
    "Luck-Gnoblar": `An Ogre with a Luck-Gnoblar may re-roll a single armour or invulnerable save, once per battle.`,
    "Look-out Gnoblar": `Any character in a unit with a Look-out Gnoblar benefits from the 'Look Out Sir!' special rule as long as there are three rank and file models of the same troop type remaining in the unit.`,
    "Name-Gnoblar": `For each Name-Gnoblar an Ogre has, he can choose an additional Big Name.`,
    "Scalp-Gnoblar": `One use only. A Butcher with a Scalp-Gnoblar may re-roll a single dice when attempting to cast a spell from the Lore of the Great Maw.`,
    "Sword-Gnoblar": `An Ogre with a Sword-Gnoblar benefits from one extra Strength 2 attack per close combat round, at the Weapon Skill of the owning model.`,
    "Tooth-Gnoblar": `One use only. After attempting to cast a spell from the Lore of the Great Maw, a Butcher with a Tooth-Gnoblar may choose to sacrifice one to get +1 to his casting value.`,
    "Their Master's Voice": `Models with this special rule can join units of War Beasts and Monstrous Beasts.`,
    "Everwinter Prayers": `A Rimespeaker knows three Prayers. They may attempt to use one at the start of each of your turns by taking a Leadership test. If passed: Call of the Blizzard (all missile fire targeting the Rimespeaker's unit suffer -1 to Hit until start of your next turn), Keening Gale (+3 Movement until start of your next turn), or Pulverising Hailstorm (all enemy units in base contact suffer D6 Strength 4 Hits).`,
    "Down to the Ironguts": `If a friendly unit of Ogres within 6" of an Irongut unit breaks from combat, the Ironguts may re-roll 1's when rolling To Hit and To Wound in close combat this turn.`,
    "Motley Crew": `The models in a unit of Maneaters can have a variety of different weapons and special rules. Opponent must state which model they want to allocate attacks to. Excess wounds carry over as normal.`,
    "Trappers": `Enemy units that successfully charge a unit of Trappers' front must take 1 Dangerous Terrain test for each Trapper in the unit as soon as the charge is completed.`,
    "Vessel of the Gulping God": `A Slaughtermaster with a Great Mawpot gains Inspiring Presence (6), Magical Ward (4+), Stubborn, +1 casting bonus, +6" range to spells. Troop type changes to War Machine; counts as part of the crew. May never voluntarily leave.`,
    "Battlebroth": `Whenever the Slaughtermaster casts an augment spell, the target unit regains 1 Wound's worth of models (as a summoning spell).`,
    "Earth-shattering Charge": `A Stonehorn has Impact Hits (D6). When it makes a successful charge, roll 2D6 and choose the highest result for the number of Impact Hits.`,
    "Stone Skeleton": `If an attack with the Multiple Wounds special rule successfully wounds a Stonehorn, halve the number of Wounds inflicted (rounding up).`,
    "Numbing Chill": `Any enemy unit within 6" of a Thundertusk has the Always Strikes Last special rule. This has no effect on models with Immunity (Ice Attacks).`,
    "Leadbelcher Gun": `Range 12/24", Strength 5, Multiple Shots (D6), Rapid Fire, Slow to Fire.`
  },

