  itemDesc: {
    "Frostfang": `The bearer gains the Ice Attacks special rule. In addition, at the start of each round of close combat, roll a D6. On a 4+, all attacks made by this weapon are increased by +1 Strength for the duration of the game. This effect is cumulative.`,
    "Thundermace": `Great weapon. The wielder may choose to exchange all of his Attacks to make a single 'Thundercrush Attack'. Roll To Hit against the highest Weapon Skill amongst enemy models in base contact. If it hits, place the small template touching the wielder's base. Infantry, war beasts or swarm models under the template suffer a single Strength 3 hit. The model under the hole suffers Strength 9 with Multiple Wounds (D3). Other troop types are unaffected.`,
    "Siegebreaker": `Great weapon. Roll To Hit against the enemy's Initiative instead of Weapon Skill, and no Parry saves are allowed. When assaulting models in a building, may make a 'Siegebreaker Attack' inflicting D6 hits with Strength equal to the building height in inches (max Strength 10).`,
    "The Tenderiser": `Great weapon. The Tenderiser gives the wielder the Multiple Wounds (D3) special rule.`,
    "Bloodcleaver": `Butcher or Slaughtermaster only. Every time the wielder causes an unsaved wound, he may regain one wound lost earlier in the battle.`,
    "The Fang of Ghur": `The wielder of this weapon gains the Frenzy special rule. In addition, no Magical Ward saves can be taken against it.`,
    "Frostshard Javelins": `Hunter only. Javelins. Attacks made with this weapon have the Ice Attacks special rule.`,
    "Sky-Titan Scatter Pistols": `Brace of Ogre Pistols. All shots from these weapons are resolved at Strength 5.`,
    "Bellowing Blade": `The wielder may re-roll one failed To Hit or To Wound roll each round of close combat for every enemy Character within 12".`,
    "Blade of All-Frost": `For every successfully Wound this weapon inflicts on an enemy Character, Monstrous Creature or Monster, that model suffers -1 Strength and Toughness for the remainder of the game.`,
    "Headsmasher": `Great weapon. Headsmasher gives the wielder the Killing Blow special rule.`,
    "Splatter-Cleaver": `Butcher or Slaughtermaster only. Every time the wielder causes an unsaved wound, they gain +1 Leadership for the duration of the close combat round.`,
    "Greedy Fist": `Ironfist. The wearer gains +1 Strength and a Magical Ward (6+). If a Magic Weapon inflicts a Wound saved by this Ward, its magical properties are consumed; treated as a non-magical weapon thereafter. An enemy Wizard loses a Wizard level and a randomly selected spell each time they are hit by an Ogre wearing the Greedy Fist.`,
    "Mastodon Armour": `Light armour. If the wearer is killed by an attack not made in close combat, roll a D6; on a 2+ they remain in play with one Wound remaining.`,
    "Gut Maw": `Gut-plate. The wearer has the Terror special rule. In addition, he recovers one lost Wound (up to his starting number) for each unsaved Wound he causes in a challenge.`,
    "Bullgut": `Model on foot only. Gut-plate. Gives the wearer Impact Hits (D3), and all Impact Hits have Armour Piercing (1).`,
    "Kattanak Browplate": `Gut-plate. The wearer gains +1 Leadership. In addition, all War Beasts and Monstrous Beasts suffer -1 To Hit against him.`,
    "Greatskull": `Gut-plate. Any Wizard that targets the bearer with a spell will miscast on any roll of any double.`,
    "Grawl's Gut-Plate": `Gut-plate. The bearer and any unit they are with adds +D3" to their charge distance while within 18" of any enemy unit.`,
    "Ice Mammoth Skull Plate": `Gut-plate. The wearer may re-roll failed armour saves.`,
    "Skullplucker": `Ironfist. Any hits made with the Skullplucker have the Killing Blow special rule.`,
    "Gnoblar Thiefstone": `Grants the bearer Magic Resistance (1). Roll D6 when deployed to see if the Thiefstone has 'found' any useful items (1: Nothing, 2: Lucky Trinket, 3: Talisman of Protection, 4: Crown of Command, 5: The Ruby Ring of Ruin, 6: Talisman of Preservation). If a character is killed in close combat while in base contact with the wearer, you may pick up any one Magic Item (except Standards) from that character.`,
    "Greyback Pelt": `Hunter only. Gives the bearer the Forest Strider, Hill Strider, Ice Attacks, and Magical Attacks special rules.`,
    "Spangleshard": `For each Wound the bearer suffers, roll a D6. If this roll is higher than the To Wound roll, that wound is ignored.`,
    "Cathayan Jet Pendant": `The bearer and any unit they join gains the Magic Resistance (3) special rule. This has no effect on spells from the Lore of Yin and Yang.`,
    "The Pelt of Charngar": `Hunter only. The bearer gains the Natural Armour (6+) and Regeneration (5+) special rules.`,
    "The Purple Rock": `Honcho only. One use per enemy Magic phase. When the enemy casts a successful spell, instead of dispelling, roll a D6: on a 4+ the spell is automatically dispelled. On a 1-3 the spell goes through and the bearer suffers a Strength 3 hit.`,
    "The Rime Shroud": `All successful To Hit rolls with missile attacks targeting the bearer must be re-rolled.`,
    "Battered Talisman": `The bearer gains a Magical Ward (4+) against Attacks with Strength 5 or more.`,
    "Red Stone": `Honcho only. The bearer gains a Magical Ward (6+) and the Magic Resistance (1) special rule.`,
    "Funny Trinket": `Honcho only. The bearer may re-roll failed armour saves and invulnerable saves.`,
    "Grubbi's Dice Bag": `Honcho only. One use only. When the bearer suffers a Wound, roll a D6. On a 2+, the Wound is ignored, as are all subsequent Wounds that turn. On a 1 the bearer is slain outright.`,
    "Shrunken Priest Head": `Butcher or Slaughtermaster only. The bearer gains a Magical Ward (5+) against the first wounding Hit each phase.`,
    "Wyrdstone Necklace": `The wearer gains a Magical Ward (5+). However, they must pass a Toughness test at the start of each of their turns or suffer a wound with no saves allowed.`,
    "Hellheart": `Charm, one use only. At the start of one of the opposing side's Magic phases, immediately after rolling for the Winds of Magic. All enemy Wizards within 12" must roll 2D6 on the Miscast table. Add one extra dispel dice to the Ogre dispel pool for each enemy Wizard forced to roll on the Miscast table.`,
    "Bangstick": `Relic. Bound Spell (Level 3, cast on 8+). Magic missile, range 24", causing 2D6 Strength 4 Hits with Flaming Attacks.`,
    "Grut's Sickle": `Relic. At the start of the Ogre Magic phase, the bearer can inflict a single Wound on any unit he has joined (distributed as a shooting attack, no saves). If he does so, he adds +2 to all casting rolls this phase. Roll 2D6 at the end of each Magic phase where used; on double 1 the unit slays the wielder.`,
    "The Hungry Maw": `Charm. One use only. Can be used after successfully dispelling an enemy spell. The enemy spell can no longer be used for the remainder of the game.`,
    "Halfling Cookbook": `Relic. May re-roll one dice (except 1's) per casting roll when using the Lore of the Great Maw.`,
    "Dragon Heart": `Charm. One use only. At the start of any of your Magic phases. For the duration of this turn, the bearer may re-roll failed casting attempts.`,
    "Flask of Congealed Maw-Juices": `Model with Great Mawpot only. Charm. One use only. At the start of any of your Magic phases. For the duration of this turn, you may add one free power dice to each of the model's casting attempts.`,
    "Bloodrock Talisman": `Relic. The bearer gains a +2 dispel bonus if they are within 12" of the casting Wizard.`,
    "Wizardflesh Apron": `Wizard with the Lore of the Great Maw only. Relic. At the start of each of your Magic phases, the bearer can pick one additional spell from the Lore of the Great Maw beyond those normally available and cast it this turn.`,
    "Tokens of the Everwinter": `One use only. At the start of any round of close combat. For the duration of this turn, the model (but not any mount) gains +1 Strength as well as Always Strikes First and Natural Armour (5+).`,
    "Brand of the Svard": `Mounted model only. The bearer's mount gains +1 To Hit in close combat.`,
    "The Seat of Alvagr": `Mounted model only. The model may make double their normal amount of Stomps.`,
    "Bleeding Skull of Dragaar": `Tyrant, Bruiser or Hunter only. The bearer can channel dispel dice in the same manner as a Level 2 Wizard.`,
    "Gnoblar Blast Keg": `Tyrant or Bruiser only. One use only. During any of your Shooting phases, place the small round template anywhere within 6" — it scatters D3". Models touched suffer Strength 3 Hit with Armour Piercing (1); model under hole suffers Strength 6 Hit with Armour Piercing (1) and Multiple Wounds (D3). Common.`,
    "Gruesome Trophy Rack": `Tyrant only. Any unit joined by this model may re-roll 1's To Hit in close combat. Common.`,
    "Shatterstone": `All enemy units within 12" of the bearer treat all terrain features as Dangerous Terrain. Terrain already Dangerous fails on a 1-2 instead of just a 1.`,
    "Brahmir Statue": `Any Psychology tests caused by the bearer (or any unit they are with) on any Beastmen unit are taken with a -3 Leadership penalty. Common.`,
    "Alvagr Rune-Tokens": `One use only. At the start of any round of close combat. The wielder gains the Ice Attacks special rule for the duration of this round. Common.`,
